  "description": "Republic of Ireland District Electoral Divisions/Wards as at 3 May 1921, assembled from Connacht (= 1919 boundaries), Leinster (= 1919 boundaries), Munster (= Apr 1907 boundaries), Ulster (outside Northern Ireland) (= 1921 boundaries). Modified version of the 1931 map. In 1931, the DEDs of Castleknock, Drumcondra Rural, Finglas, Howth Rural, Palmerston, Rathfarnham and Terenure were split by the expansion of Dublin county borough. Additionally, on October 1st 1921, following the formation of Passage West Urban District, the DED of Monkstown was split into Monkstown Rural and Monkstown Urban. This latter change is not recorded on a separate map as Paddy has already created one.",
